; bqmx_exceeds_memory_budget: an allocation past the budget must fault
; with MemoryLimitExceeded, at the same instruction and with no allocation.
;
; 2^30 variables at 8 bytes each is 8 GiB against the 1 GiB
; default, so BQMX raises MemoryLimitExceeded on the charge and never
; reaches the allocation. Three instructions, no calldata.
;
; The fault is MemoryLimitExceeded and not InvalidAllocation: the size is
; a valid allocation request (non-negative, and representable as a usize
; on a 64-bit target), it is simply larger than the budget. The charge is
; taken off the i64 before the usize conversion precisely so this
; identity is the same on wasm32, where the conversion would otherwise
; decide it.

PUSH 1073741824
BQMX r0
HALT
